   <text>
      <body>
         <div type="letter">
                <div type="address">
                    <ab>
                        <address>
                            <addrLine>
                                <name type="geo" key="G_CHE_ZURI_09">Universitätstrasse 29 III</name>
                            </addrLine>
                            <addrLine>
                                <name type="geo" key="G_CHE_ZURI">Zurich</name>
                            </addrLine> </address>
                    </ab>
                </div>
                <div type="mainBody">
                    <p>Dear <name type="person" key="weav76">Miss Weaver</name>: I send you also <seg xml:id="seg1" type="note-anchor">a paper</seg> just received from <name type="geo" key="G_AUT_VIEN">Vienna</name> which mentions a still stranger case of ‘coincidence’. The story alluded to in the second paragraph is <hi rend="underline">A</hi> <hi rend="underline">Painful</hi> <hi rend="underline">Case</hi> in <name type="work" key="W_DUBLINERS">
                            <hi rend="underline">Dubliners</hi>
                        </name>.</p>
                    <closer>
                        <salute>        	With kind regards</salute>
                        <salute>                    	sincerely yours</salute>
                        <signed>                                	<name type="person" key="joyc82">James Joyce</name>
                        </signed>
                        <dateline>
                            <date when="1919-08-28">28/8/919</date>
                        </dateline>
                    </closer>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div type="notes">
                <note xml:id="note1" target="#seg1" type="commentary">
                    <rs type="letter" key="L_68698">JJ wrote to Harriet Weaver on 9 December 1920</rs>: “In one of your letters, which I cannot refer to here, you mentioned some book or writings of — on the subject of prophecy. It was in connection with the articles in a Viennese paper about the coincidence of <hi rend="italic">A Painful Case</hi>. May I ask you for the name of the writer?” (<name type="work">LI</name> 151).</note>
            </div>
      </body>
   </text>
